{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>Assemble to me.</b> They did not sound the trumpets that day to assemble the congregation, because it says (Numbers 10) ״Make for yourself,״ and he did not give Joshua authority over them, and even in his lifetime they were hidden away — on the day of his death — to fulfill what is said (Ecclesiastes 8) ״and there is no authority on the day of death״ (Tanchuma Vayechi and Beha'alotcha)." "<b>And I will testify against them the heavens and the earth.</b> And if you say, behold he has already testified above — ״I call as witness against you this day״? There he said it to Israel, but to the heavens and to the earth he did not say; and now he comes to say ״Give ear, O heavens״ (Deuteronomy 32)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:06.467161164Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}